        <p class="eyebrow">Cat Care FAQ</p>
        <h1 id="page-title">Everything you meant to ask about cats</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Quick answers to the most common cat questions, from purring and naps to
          litter boxes and why your cat suddenly sprints down the hallway at 3 a.m.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="hero-card" aria-label="At a glance">
        <div class="stat">
          <span>Audience</span>
          <strong>Cat people and future cat people</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span>Format</span>
          <strong>Tap or press Enter / Space to expand</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span>Design</span>
          <strong>Modern, calm, and easy to scan</strong>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <h2 id="faq-title" class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;left:-9999px;">Frequently asked questions</h2>

      <div class="example">
        <h3>
          <button type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="question">
              <strong>Why do cats purr?</strong>
              <span>It’s not always just happiness.</span>
            </span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details">
          <p>Cats purr for comfort, communication, and sometimes self-soothing when they feel nervous or unwell.</p>
          <p>A relaxed cat usually purrs because they feel safe, but the same sound can also show up during recovery, feeding, or attention-seeking.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h3>
          <button type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="question">
              <strong>How much should I feed my cat?</strong>
              <span>It depends on age, size, and activity.</span>
            </span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details">
          <p>Start with the feeding guide on your cat’s food and adjust based on body condition, energy level, and your vet’s advice.</p>
          <p>Kittens usually need more frequent meals, while adult cats do well with consistent portions and a regular schedule.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h3>
          <button type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="question">
              <strong>Why do cats knead blankets?</strong>
              <span>It’s a cozy habit with kitten roots.</span>
            </span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details">
          <p>Kneading is often a sign of comfort. Many cats keep the behavior from kittenhood, when kneading helped stimulate milk flow.</p>
          <p>Adult cats may knead to relax, mark territory with scent glands in their paws, or settle in before a nap.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h3>
          <button type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="question">
              <strong>Do indoor cats need enrichment?</strong>
              <span>Yes — curiosity needs an outlet.</span>
            </span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details">
          <p>Absolutely. Indoor cats stay healthier and happier when they can climb, scratch, hunt, and explore.</p>
          <p>Rotate toys, add vertical spaces, and use short play sessions to mimic the hunt-rest-repeat rhythm cats naturally enjoy.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h3>
          <button type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="question">
              <strong>Why do cats zoom around at night?</strong>
              <span>They’re built for short bursts of energy.</span>
            </span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details">
          <p>Nighttime bursts often come from pent-up energy, hunting instincts, or a schedule that doesn’t quite match yours.</p>
          <p>A good play session before bed and a predictable routine can help redirect the midnight sprinting.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll(".example").forEach((item) => {
      const button = item.querySelector("button");
      const panel = item.querySelector(".details");

      button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
      panel.hidden = true;

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const expanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!expanded));
        panel.hidden = expanded;
      });
    });
  </script>
